
# proptest seeds for failing cases. Deliberately NOT tracked.
#
# proptest saves a seed on every failure and replays it forever. That is right
# for a real bug and wrong for a flaky assertion: a legitimate 1-in-256
# collision in prop_shamir_split_uses_fresh_randomness got saved and, on a
# reused CI workspace, turned into a permanent red that blocked deploys. The
# assertion is fixed; keeping the directory untracked stops a future false
# positive from becoming sticky the same way.
proptest-regressions/
# BOTH spellings. 84182ca ignored only the dotless form, which is what current
# proptest writes (pipeline #8 saved to api/rust/proptest-regressions/). But the
# repo also carried a legacy dot-prefixed .proptest-regressions/ -- deleted by
# hand in d17568a -- so the ignore missed it entirely and it could have become
# sticky again exactly the same way.
.proptest-regressions/
